  <prompt>
    Write Jest + React Testing Library unit tests covering the W2 send-side surface: the `&lt;EmailComposer /&gt;` engine (reducer, validation, modes, imperative handle), the sub-components (RecipientField normalization, AttachmentList caps), the three wrappers (mount-locking + prop pass-through), and `communicationApi.ts` (`SendCommunicationError` parsing + one-shot deprecation warn). Follow ADR-038 KEEP-path categories and the existing `@spaarke/ui-components` Jest setup; mock at the boundary (`communicationApi.sendCommunication`, `Xrm.WebApi`, `searchUsersAndContacts`) — do NOT mock React internals or over-mock.

    Test files to create under `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/__tests__/` (+ `services/__tests__/`):

    1. `EmailComposer.reducer.test.ts` — initial state per mode (compose/view/reply/forward/draft); `SET_FIELD`, `ADD_/REMOVE_/TOGGLE_ATTACHMENT`, `SET_MODE` transition matrix (view→reply, view→forward, view→compose, compose→draft), `BEGIN_/END_SEND` toggling isSending, `RESET`.
    2. `validation.test.ts` — every canonical code triggered once: `TO_REQUIRED`, `TO_INVALID_EMAIL`, `TO_TOO_MANY`, `SUBJECT_REQUIRED`, `BODY_REQUIRED`, `ATTACHMENT_TOO_LARGE`, `ATTACHMENTS_TOO_MANY`, `ATTACHMENT_BLOCKED_TYPE`, `FROM_REQUIRED`, `FROM_NOT_APPROVED`; `forSend=false` skips SUBJECT/BODY required.
    3. `RecipientField.test.tsx` — paste `"Alice &lt;alice@example.com&gt;; bob@example.com,charlie@example.com"` → 3 Tags (the canonical `;`/`,`/mixed normalization); invalid email + Enter → no Tag + TO_INVALID_EMAIL; Backspace removes last Tag; aria-labels for To/Cc/Bcc.
    4. `AttachmentList.test.tsx` — 150-cap → ATTACHMENTS_TOO_MANY + Add disabled; 35 MB total → ATTACHMENT_TOO_LARGE; 25 MB → soft warning MessageBar (no hard block); source badges per kind; remove; forward-mode selection checkbox toggles TOGGLE_ATTACHMENT_SELECTED.
    5. `modes.test.ts` — `dedupSubjectPrefix` (Re:/Fwd:/FW:, case-insensitive, no double prefix); `deriveReplyState` (to=original from, cc=[], `Re:` subject, wrapped body, associations carried); `deriveForwardState` (blank to, `Fwd:`, attachments carried selected); `deriveDraftState` (existingCommunicationId + `mapStateToDraftUpdate` shape).
    6. `imperative-handle.test.tsx` — render `&lt;EmailComposer ref /&gt;`; `getState()`, `validate()`, `send()` (mocked `sendCommunication`), `saveDraft()`.
    7. `wrappers.test.tsx` — `SendEmailStep` locks `mount='inline'` + forwards `composerRef`; `SendEmailDialog` locks `mount='dialog'` + `onSent`→onClose; `SendEmailPage` locks `mount='page'` + requires `mode`, `onClose`→onCancel.
    8. `services/__tests__/communicationApi.test.ts` — `SendCommunicationError.fromResponse` parses ProblemDetails (status/code/detail/correlationId) + falls back on non-JSON; `sendCommunication()` throws `SendCommunicationError` on non-2xx; one-shot deprecation warn fires exactly once across multiple `attachmentDocumentIds` calls.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    React + TypeScript developer with Jest + React Testing Library + reducer-testing experience; fluent in boundary-mocking and ADR-038 KEEP-path test classification.
  </role>

  <goal>
    All test files green under `npm run test` in `@spaarke/ui-components`. Every canonical validation code exercised once; recipient `;`/`,`/mixed parsing tested; attachment caps tested at boundaries (150 / 35 MB / 25 MB); mode pre-fill helpers covered; imperative handle covered; wrapper mount-locking covered; `SendCommunicationError` parsing + one-shot deprecation warn covered. Coverage of `EmailComposer/` ≥ 80% lines. Tests are MAINTAIN-class per ADR-038 (behavior contracts, not scaffolding).
  </goal>

